Package: ConDAdistV4
Title: Consensus Differential Abundance With Configurable P-Value Combination (V4)
Version: 0.4.1
Authors@R:
    person("Heekuk", "Park", email = "hp2523@cumc.columbia.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Unified JSD-line CDD core that subsumes ConDA-dist V1_JSD and
    V2_JSD as a single V4 implementation. The main user-facing switch is the
    p-value combiner used for DA consensus: adaptive-truncated Cauchy
    (recommended default) or Fisher (legacy-style). Internally, Fisher uses
    V1_JSD-style consensus and SIMPER+LOO beta contribution, while
    adaptive-truncated Cauchy uses V2_JSD-style consensus and LOO-only beta
    contribution.
